    "title": "Commerce Department Blocks Natcast CHIPS Funding",
    "text": "The U.S. Commerce Department has abruptly shifted operational control of the National Semiconductor Technology Center (NSTC) from the nonprofit Natcast to the National Institute of Standards and Technology (NIST). This move effectively scraps a US $7.4 billion agreement intended to fund research and growth for advanced semiconductor technology under the U.S. CHIPS and Science Act .\ncommerce Department Rejects Natcast Funding, Cites Legal Requirements The U.S. Commerce Department will not fund the CHIPS Act’s R&D through Natcast, its previously designated nonprofit administrator. Operational control has been transferred to NIST.\nThe Commerce Department",
